      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2015,
      "text": "Consider the following two statements. - $S_{1}$: If a candidate is known to be corrupt, then he will not be elected - $S_{2}$: If a candidate is kind, he will be elected Which one of the following statements follows from $S_{1}$ and $S_{2}$ as per sound inference rules of logic?",
      "options": [
        "If a person is known to be corrupt, he is kind",
        "If a person is not known to be corrupt, he is not kind",
        "If a person is kind, he is not known to be corrupt",
        "If a person is not kind, he is not known to be corrupt"
      ],
      "answer": [
        2
      ],
