      "text": "Three sisters $(R, S, \\text{and} T)$ received a total of 24 toys during Christmas. The toys were initially divided among them in a certain proportion. Subsequently, $R$ gave some toys to $S$ which doubled the share of $S$. Then $S$ in turn gave some of her toys to $T$, which doubled $T'$ 's share. Next, some of $T'$ 's toys were given to $R$, which doubled the number of toys that $R$ currently had. As a result of all such exchanges, the three sisters were left with equal number of toys. How many toys did $R$ have originally?",
      "options": [
        "8",
        "9",
        "11",
        "12"
      ],
