      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2010,
      "text": "A tank has 100 liters of water. At the end of every hour, the following two operations are performed in sequence: i) water equal to $m\\%$ of the current contents of the tank is added to the tank, ii) water equal to $n\\%$ of the current contents of the tank is removed from the tank. At the end of 5 hours, the tank contains exactly 100 liters of water. The relation between $m$ and $n$ is:",
      "options": [
        "m = n",
        "$m > n$",
        "m < n",
        "None of the previous"
      ],
      "answer": [
