      "text": "For positive real numbers $S$ and $K$, the function $H_K(S)$ is defined as: $H_{K}(S) = \\max (S - K,0)$. The max function is defined as: $\\max (a, b) = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l l} a, & \\text {when} a > b \\\\ b, & \\text {when} a \\leq b \\end{array} \\right.$ The graph below shows the plot of a function $N(S)$ versus $S$. $N(S)$ can be expressed as \\_\\_\\_\\_.",
      "options": [
        "$H_{10}(S) - H_{20}(S)$",
        "$H_{10}(S) - 2H_{20}(S)$",
