        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-7",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "year": 2014,
      "text": "A dance programme is scheduled for 10.00 a.m. Some students are participating in the programme and they need to come an hour earlier than the start of the event. These students should be accompanied by a parent. Other students and parents should come in time for the programme. The instruction you think that is appropriate for this is",
      "options": [
        "Students should come at 9.00 a.m. and parents should come at 10.00 a.m.",
        "Participating students should come at 9.00 a.m. accompanied by a parent, and other parents and students should come by 10.00 a.m.",
        "Students who are not participating should come by 10.00 a.m. and they should not bring their parents. Participating students should come at 9.00 a.m.",
        "Participating students should come before 9.00 a.m. Parents who accompany them should come at 9.00 a.m. All others should come at 10.00 a.m."
      ],
      "answer": [
        1
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.7",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2014 | Set 3 | GA | Question: 6",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "6",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse-2014-set3",
          "verbal-aptitude",
          "passage-reading",
          "easy"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-8",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "year": 2014,
      "text": "By the beginning of the $20^{th}$ century, several hypotheses were being proposed, suggesting a paradigm shift in our understanding of the universe. However, the clinching evidence was provided by experimental measurements of the position of a star which was directly behind our sun. Which of the following inference(s) may be drawn from the above passage? i. Our understanding of the universe changes based on the positions of stars ii. Paradigm shifts usually occur at the beginning of centuries iii. Stars are important objects in the universe iv. Experimental evidence was important in confirming this paradigm shift",
      "options": [
        "i, ii and iv",
        "iii only",
        "i and iv",
        "iv only"
      ],
      "answer": [
        3
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.8",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2014 | Set 3 | GA | Question: 7",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "7",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse-2014-set3",
          "verbal-aptitude",
          "passage-reading",
          "easy"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-9",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2015,
      "text": "Most experts feel that in spite of possessing all the technical skills required to be a batsman of the highest order, he is unlikely to be so due to lack of requisite temperament. He was guilty of throwing away his wicket several time after working hard to lay a strong foundation. His critics pointed out that until he addressed his problem, success at the highest level will continue to elude him. Which of the statement(s) below is/are logically valid and can be inferred from the above passage? i. He was already a successful batsman at the highest level. ii. He was to improve his temperament in order to become a great batsman. iii. He failed to make many of his good starts count. iv. Improving his technical skills will guarantee success.",
      "options": [
        "iii and iv",
        "ii and iii",
        "i, ii and iii",
        "ii only"
      ],
      "answer": [
        1
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.9",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2015 | Set 3 | GA | Question: 9",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "9",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse-2015-set3",
          "verbal-aptitude",
          "normal",
          "passage-reading"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-10",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2016,
      "text": "Computers were invented for performing only high-end useful computations. However, it is no understatement that they have taken over our world today. The internet, for example, is ubiquitous. Many believe that the internet itself is an unintended consequence of the original invention. With the advent of mobile computing on our phones, a whole new dimension is now enabled. One is left wondering if all these developments are good or, more importantly, required. Which of the statement(s) below is/are logically valid and can be inferred from the above paragraph? (i) The author believes that computers are not good for us. (ii) Mobile computers and the internet are both intended inventions.",
      "options": [
        "(i) only",
        "(ii) only",
        "Both (i) and (ii)",
        "Neither (i) nor (ii)"
      ],
      "answer": [
        3
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.10",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2016 | Set 2 | GA | Question: 07",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "07",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse-2016-set2",
          "verbal-aptitude",
          "passage-reading",
          "normal"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-11",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2017,
      "text": "\"The hold of the nationalist imagination on our colonial past is such that anything inadequately or improperly nationalist is just not history.\" Which of the following statements best reflects the author's opinion?",
      "options": [
        "Nationalists are highly imaginative.",
        "History is viewed through the filter of nationalism.",
        "Our colonial past never happened.",
        "Nationalism has to be both adequately and properly imagined."
      ],
      "answer": [
        1
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.11",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2017 | Set 1 | GA | Question: 6",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "6",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse-2017-set1",
          "general-aptitude",
          "verbal-aptitude",
          "passage-reading"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-12",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2022,
      "text": "Some people believe that “what gets measured, improves”. Some others believe that “what gets measured, gets gamed”. One possible reason for the difference in the beliefs is the work culture in organizations. In organizations with good work culture, metrics help improve outcomes. However, the same metrics are counterproductive in organizations with poor work culture. Which one of the following is the CORRECT logical inference based on the information in the above passage?",
      "options": [
        "Metrics are useful in organizations with poor work culture",
        "Metrics are useful in organizations with good work culture",
        "Metrics are always counterproductive in organizations with good work culture",
        "Metrics are never useful in organizations with good work culture"
      ],
      "answer": [
        1
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.12",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2022 | GA | Question: 6",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "6",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse-2022",
          "verbal-aptitude",
          "passage-reading",
          "two-marks"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-13",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2025,
      "text": "\"I put the brown paper in my pocket along with the chalks, and possibly other things. I suppose every one must have reflected how primeval and how poetical are the things that one carries in one's pocket: the pocket-knife, for instance the type of all human tools, the infant of the sword. Once I planned to write a b poems entirely about the things in my pocket. But I found it would be too long: and the age of the great e past.\" (From G.K. Chesterton's \"A Piece of Chalk\") Based only on the information provided in the above passage, which one of the following statements is true?",
      "options": [
        "The author of the passage carries a mirror in his pocket to reflect upon things.",
        "The author of the passage had decided to write a poem on epics.",
        "The pocket-knife is described as the infant of the sword.",
        "Epics are described as too inconvenient to write."
      ],
      "answer": [
        2
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.13",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2025 | Set 1 | GA | Question: 6",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "6",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse2025-set1",
          "verbal-aptitude",
          "passage-reading",
          "two-marks"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-14",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2010,
      "text": "The ban on smoking in designated public places can save a large number of people from the well-known effects of environmental tobacco smoke. Passive smoking seriously impairs respiratory health. The ban rightly seeks to protect non-smokers from its ill effects. Which of the following statements best sums up the meaning of the above passage:",
      "options": [
        "Effects of environmental tobacco are well known.",
        "The ban on smoking in public places protects the non-smokers.",
        "Passive smoking is bad for health.",
        "The ban on smoking in public places excludes passive smoking."
      ],
      "answer": [
        1
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume1.pdf",
        "volume": "vol1",
        "ref": "11.9.14",
        "exam": "GATE2010 MN: GA-6",
        "section": "Passage Reading",
        "paper_question": "",
        "tags": [],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mineru-vol1-11-9-15",
      "topic": "verbal",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2010,
      "text": "It has taken fifty-six long and frustrating, years to turn bronze, into gold for India's Olympics aspirations. Beijing 2008 marks a defining moment in India's Olympic history. From Delhi to Beijing is a long journey but one that our Olympians have undertaken with courage. Which of the following statement best sums up the meaning of the above passage:",
      "options": [
        "India's participation in Olympics has been frustrating.",
        "Beijing Olympics was a landmark in India's Olympic history.",
        "Our Olympians have undertaken a long journey to Beijing.",
        "India's bronze medal turned into gold at Beijing."
      ],
      "answer": [
        1
      ],
      "origin": {
