      "year": 2017,
      "text": "\"We lived in a culture that denied any merit to literary works, considering them important only when they were handmaidens to something seemingly more urgent – namely ideology. This was a country where all gestures, even the most private, were interpreted in political terms.\" The author's belief that ideology is not as important as literature is revealed by the word:",
